{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/124192-your-dreaming-house-rules","id":124192,"title":"Your Dreaming House Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-02T18:40:59-07:00","id":124192,"title":"Your Dreaming House Rules","content":"I've been brewing some changes to the dreaming rules and I'm curious to hear what others have changed for their own games and why they made those changes. So whether you're an ST or player, please share! Thanks. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T05:28:55-07:00","id":124424,"title":"","content":"What's wrong with the rules? I mean I've had to work on the contracts but the system is surprisingly solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:08:06-07:00","id":124615,"title":"","content":"There are many things about the system that work pretty well, but for my group it seems to have come time to experiment with a few things. We've been doing more and more dream work in our games and while it's been fun, we've run up against a few sticking points repeatedly. <br /> <br /> The meditation roll to get into a dream besides the character's own in the first place has been so clunky as to pretty much never get used. We understand the reasoning behind it, but it gets old and boring fast and seems to undermine the special bond that a pledgebound dream task brings. It also tends to be narratively far less interesting.<br /> <br /> Leaving so many dream maneuvers to a Wits + Empathy + Wyrd roll never really seemed right, since it the basic rules tie certain types of maneuvers to different stats. Longer-term analysis rolls (like analyzing the dreamer would be) fall under Intelligence, for example. Convincing the dreamer has more to do with Manipulation than Wits, and so on. I understand that one roll simplifies the situation and allows players to stack their characters accordingly, but it makes more sense to me that changelings might be better at certain maneuvers than others.<br /> <br /> Further, I've been tinkering with restructuring the basic categories of dreams. Dream riding claims to be for maneuvers which cause small changes and mostly leaving the dream intact, but not all of the maneuvers listed change anything (learning about the dreamer) and some would seem to change more than a little in the end (psychotherapy). A fairly obvious and strong pattern that does seem to emerge is that some maneuvers are almost purely analytical (analyzing, learning, and searching for poison), others are more manipulative (for good and for ill, from convincing to siphoning glamour to nightmares), and yet others are based around moves that are purely beneficial to the recipient (scouring, healing, psychotherapy).<br /> <br /> And while I understand the idea behind changing a dream too much and ripping it apart, it's always seemed to penalize good rolls that players otherwise get excited about and which do not usually hurt the scene in any real way. So I'm pondering changes to that.<br /> <br /> I'm less interested in arguing about such things than seeing what others might have changed for their groups and why, and how things played out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T17:34:35-07:00","id":126283,"title":"","content":"Rather<br /> <br /> I changed the rules for entering dreams, mostly because I thought that the idea of the Pathfinder clause of the Contracts of Dream were dodgy as hell. Instead of entering dreams being a 'default' fae power (not True Fae power, mind), I made that the first Clause of Dream. The 'Pathfinder' power became a default power for changelings who were taught it, sort of a little trick that came with learning how to open doors to the Hedge...<br /> <br /> Other than that, though, I didn't find myself <i>changing</i> much at all, but I tweaked a few things (see below). The above change DID alter some basic assumptions about the game (e.g. Oneiromancy became more niche than universal), but it worked well enough for my troupe. Reading <b>KismetRose</b>'s description of dream mechanics being clunky, I'd tend to agree. My alteration, in all honesty, really helped me to keep my troupe from needing to use dreams long enough for ME to get a handle on them.<br /> <br /> Any day now, I should have those rules down pat! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Tweaks I made include:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Choosing a Kith that doesn't match the Seeming is easy for my troupe, but the combination HAS to fit with the character. So we have a Wizened Antiquarian, which is an easy fit, and a Darkling Oracle, which really works for that character. I allowed a player to pitch her Fairest Gargantuan, but we decided that she really wanted to play a Draconic. I'm willing to bend those rules as needed for a character.<br /> <br /> \u2022 I'm very broad minded about what emotions fall into the purview of the Seasonal Courts. King Spring in my city, as an example, embodies the desire for home, for the comforts that come with belonging. That's NOT what most of us think when we think of the Antler Crown, but it fits wonderfully with how the Court could work. My partner's character is Summer Court, an odd choice I thought since her character was a very caring individual, but when she told me that his wrath is directed at the monster he once was \u2013 a complicated tale of complicity with multiple Gentry \u2013 I allowed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T19:36:25-07:00","id":126363,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/124192-your-dreaming-house-rules?p=126283#post126283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I changed the rules for entering dreams, mostly because I thought that the idea of the Pathfinder clause of the Contracts of Dream were dodgy as hell. Instead of entering dreams being a 'default' fae power (not True Fae power, mind), I made that the first Clause of Dream. The 'Pathfinder' power became a default power for changelings who were taught it, sort of a little trick that came with learning how to open doors to the Hedge...</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting! I can see how that would work like a charm if you wanted a gate to dreamwork instead of having it as a baseline ability. Thank you for sharing that change and your rationale, and even telling me how it played out for your group!<br /> <br /> I'm coming at it from the other end: We love dreamwork and want to make it more accessible and usable by more types of fae than those who directly stack Wits + Empathy + Wyrd for it. For instance, one of the changes I'm going to playtest is the notion that changelings don't suffer from their seeming curse in dreams. If only in their dreams, they can be what they imagine themselves to be. That's only a small change, however; one of many small adjustments I've been working on.<br /> <br /> On the grander side, I'm recategorizing the dream maneuvers (instead of dream riding, dreamscaping, and dream weaving) and changing the rolls for many maneuvers so they reflect the stats most associated with those types of actions within the baseline system. For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Learn about the Dreamer:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Intelligence + Empathy + Wyrd \u2013 Intensity. Each roll takes all night. Normally, every five successes allows you to learn one aspect of your choice: Virtue, Vice, permanent Willlpower rating, Derangements (one per 5 successes), Merits (Mental and Social only), Flaws (Mental and Social only), or any mental or emotional supernatural power used on dreamer within the last month. However, it only takes three successes to learn the following information: Virtue and Vice from wish fulfillment dreams; permanent Willpower rating from memory dreams; derangements from nightmares; Merits and Flaws from recurring memory dreams; and supernatural powers used on the dreamer from recurring dreams.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The roll is new, based on the baseline system's standard of rolling Intelligence for analysis actions. The middle is pretty much as per the core. The last part assigns some unintended bonuses that can be gained from sitting in on the different types of dreams mentioned in the core.<br /> <br /> Other changes are for clarification purposes. For instance, who can be affected by a dream vessel. First the core says &quot;any dreamer may experience the dream -- not simply one to whom its creator is bound by Wyrd.&quot; Then it says it &quot;may be used by any changeling, fetch, or human bound in a dreaming-tasked pledge.&quot; The first sentence implies ANY dreamer, not just the fae or their pledgebound; the next sentence restricts it back to those who are essentially already touched by the Wyrd. So which is it? For us, it's ANY dreamer, including other supernatural types (though they add their power stat to resist an unknown vessel).<br /> <br /> I love this game so much it ain't even funny and we play the hell out of it, which is why I'm doing this. =)</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T11:05:09-07:00","id":126811,"title":"","content":"One thing that I read somewhere and tinkered with a little was allowing changelings to enter dreams of people they've shared pledges with as long as they're in the general vicinity of the dreamer (usually the same room). the meditation is still an option for people who can't get close enough to do it the normal way, but this provides a less clunky option. I've also considered moving the required successes down a bit as 16 successes at I think a half hour per roll makes dream riding more tedious and time consuming than such a major part of the game has any right to be, but I haven't experimented much with that yet. maybe 5 successes for the fetch and 10 for pledge dreams.<br /> <br /> I've also given dream-centric fairies the ability to cause bashing damage when attacking a dreamer, with the option to do lethal when they spend a willpower. Not too much to say on that one, I just feel like after I've given a fairy the name &quot;Morpheus, King of Nightmares&quot; he should be able to pull a freddy krueger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T09:59:22-07:00","id":128337,"title":"","content":"Very rarely are the changelings in my game within the same vicinity as their pledges when they go to sleep, but I can see how allowing entry that way would work if you didn't want to abandon the entry roll altogether. I can also understand wanting to reduce the number of required successes to speed things along. <br /> <br /> While dreaming can be a very important part of a session, the entry roll got to be so repetitive and annoying that we let go of it quickly. We've been playing it that dream maneuvers take all night to accomplish and the changelings always clear their schedules with that in mind, so figuring out how long it takes to get into the dream becomes a moot point. (And if the dream gets interrupted, it gets interrupted.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}